  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">a). Number of states in which Gram Panchayats prepare integrated plans focusing on SDGs.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2018">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">a) 0</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. State governments localise SDGs targets and integrate into state and district planning process
2. Strengthening the monitoring and evaluation of SDGs by institutionalizing the digital tools
3. Strengthening the State Capacities by supporting in improving the public service Delivery
4. Technical Support to State Governments through Government funding</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Around 25 States has prepared their State Indicator Framework and integrated their Plans. The Localisation at the Gram Panchayat level didn&#x2019;t happened due to COVID outbreak. 
2. UNDP has prepared/launched SDG monitoring tool for Uttarakhand, Punjab etc. 
3. UNDP has improved the scheme implementation performance of Rural Housing in Odisha, SRLM in Uttarakhand and Karnataka, Skill Development schemes in Uttarakhand etc. 
4. UNDP has initiated technical support to Department of Skills &amp; Employment, Government of Uttarakhand in implementing the Sankalp Project in the year 2021.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Establish 3 SDG Coordination Centres (SDGCC) (Karnataka, Jammu and Kashmir and Maharashtra) 
2. Support NITI Aayog in conducting 3 regional review meetings to measure progress and fast track implementation of SDGs
3. Launch SDG monitoring and evaluation dashboard in 3 states (Haryana, Nagaland and Uttarakhand)</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Established SDGCC in Karnataka; proposal for SDGCCs in Maharashtra and Jammu and Kashmir have been delayed due to COVID-19
2. Regional review for the Northeast undertaken with participation of 8 states and a blue print for fast tracking implementation and achievement of SDGs prepared. The rest of the reviews have been rescheduled due to COVID-19.
3. SDG monitoring and evaluation dashboard launched in Uttarakhand</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. State governments localise SDGs targets and integrate into state and district planning process 
2. Strengthening the monitoring and evaluation of SDGs by institutionalizing the digital tools
3. Mobilising Private Sector partners for focused activities on SDGs
4. Information Education Communication and Knowledge Management for SDGs
5. Strengthening the State Capacities by supporting in improving the public service Delivery</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">A. Technical support to Union Territories for SDG implementation
1.	UNDP supported MoSPI in organising 3 UT level workshops for development and review of UT Indicator Framework at Chandigarh (Chandigarh, Ladakh, J&amp;K, Delhi), Daman (D&amp;N Haveli and Daman and Diu) and Port Blair (A&amp;N islands, Puducherry). 
2.	Provided technical support for &#x201c;National Workshop on Developing/Reviewing Sub-National Level Monitoring Framework for SDGs&#x201d; at Delhi on 31st October 2022. The workshop was attended by more than 100 people.
3.	Technical support to UT of Dadra and Nagar Haveli and Daman and Diu for preparation of Vision Document 2030

B. Technical support to NITI Aayog:
1.	Technical support to NITI Aayog in drafting the report titled &#x201c;The Indian Model of SDG Localisation&#x201d;
2.	Technical support to NITI Aayog in conducting 18 State Workshops in 18 State Capitals on SDG Monitoring and Localisation.
3.	UNDP assisting 112 aspirational districts in formulating proposals to access funds under Externally Aided Programme (EAP) of SDGs &#x2013; 50 District level proposals reviewed and placed for EC in 2022.

C. UNDP&#x2019;s support for SDGCC in states
1.	SDGCC in Tamil Nadu has been approved by the state and LPAC done. Draft MoA shared and the classifications for the positions at SDGCC Tamil Nadu has been submitted.
2.	SDGCC in J&amp;K approved and MoA to be signed. A one- day workshop was organized in Jammu for accelerating SDGs in the UT. The workshop was attended by more than 50 people from the line departments. 

D. UNDP India- UNDP Seoul Policy Centre Partnership (USPC) 
1.	Technical webinars and e-consultations to share experience, knowledge and good practices organized with USPC, the government of ROK, LSAK, UNOSSC, UNDP Rwanda and UNDP Bangladesh
2.	A digital repository on the SDGs &#x2013; the SDG Knowledge Hub &#x2013; designed and developed for knowledge exchange
3.	Country&#x2019;s first certified e-learning course on the SDGs developed with 5 modules (each with 4 sub-modules), entry and exit survey, graded assessment test and a voluntary SDG pledge. 
4.	Country wide good practices across the 17 SDGs and UNDP&#x2019;s COVID-19 response documented 

E. State Outreach activities
1.	Supported SDG Dashboard development for Nagaland, Maharashtra
2.	A consultation was organized with Start-ups in Odisha to highlight their role in achieving the SDGs. The consultation was organized by 60 start-ups.
3.	CSR Matchmaking Platform support to Pune Municipality</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
